{"type":"text","timestamp":1793589462477,"sessionID":"ses_e65be63cdffe7X56IjpBNFOOkc","part":{"id":"prt_19a42f38d001v4iEFxxgRmRrKt_text-0","sessionID":"ses_e65be63cdffe7X56IjpBNFOOkc","messageID":"msg_19a42f38d001v4iEFxxgRmRrKt","type":"text","text":"Done. Everything is green and verified.\n\n## What I found\n\nThe integration test computes `(900 + 5×75) × 1.25 = 1593.75 → 1590` credits on top of 100, persisted across save/load. Three separate causes each broke that flow — the test only surfaced their combined effect:\n\n1. **Config precedence inverted** (`arena_server/config/loader.py`) — env vars were applied *before* the JSON file, so the file clobbered `ARENA_KILL_BONUS` (75 became 50 → payout 1440). `docs/CONFIG.md` says env always wins. Fix: apply file first, then env on top. I also widened the env scan from `DEFAULTS` keys to merged `cfg` keys and coerce against the current value, so a key introduced only by the file still gets its env override and the right type.\n\n2. **Credits dropped on load** (`arena_server/persistence/codec.py`) — `encode` wrote `credits` but `decode` never read it back, so profiles silently reset to 0, violating \"credits … survive save/load\". Fix: restore `credits` in `decode`.\n\n3. **Rounding was float-fragile** (`arena_server/economy/payout.py`) — `math.floor(raw/10 + 0.5)` happens to work for exactly-representable halves but binary float drift (e.g. a raw of `…4.4999999` from a percentage multiplier) rounds halves the wrong way, violating \"halves always rounding up\". Fix: `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP` to the nearest ten. (Stdlib only — no new dependencies; `legacy_payout.py` is documented as unused by live economy, so I left it.)\n\n## How I know it's right\n\n- `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` → **13 tests, OK** (integration included); tests were not modified.\n- Direct checks against the docs: env beats file with file supplying `event_multiplier` (`kill_bonus=75` in merged cfg), doc example `1585 → 1590`, exact-half and float-drift edge inputs round up correctly, and the integration test passes run in isolation.\n\n**Assumptions:** the failing test is the match flow above; \"fix every cause\" means all deviations from `docs/` on this path, not speculative modules (untouched per-module files like `store/`, `telemetry/` have their own passing unit tests).","time":{"start":1793589441424,"end":1793589462477}}}
